# The named baseline for the mixed TSan tree's noise — same discipline as
# lint-baseline.txt: what is listed here is machine-absorbed, and anything NEW
# (any report whose stack names a C++ frame of ours) still fails the run.
#
# Why the noise exists: the tree instruments the C++ shell and leaves the Rust
# engine uninstrumented (measured, not taste — see the QIMGV_SANITIZERS block
# in the root CMakeLists.txt). Every report the mixed binary produces names the
# uninstrumented side: a qimgv_engine symbol, or Rust std internals
# (library/alloc, library/core) reached through memcpy interception, with no
# ordering visible to either access. A real cross-boundary race is invisible
# here regardless — the boundary is covered by the sole-writer contract and
# architecture_rules.py, and the engine's own surface is measured on its own
# runtime — so suppressing by these frame shapes hides nothing that was
# decidable.
race:qimgv_engine
race:library/alloc/src
race:library/core/src

# Third-party internals with our frames only as the caller: glibc's own
# timezone-init race (first localtime/tzset from a worker thread), and libpng's
# row writer colliding with an already-dead thread's memcpy — the thread whose
# death pthread_clockjoin_np never recorded, so TSan still counts it live.
race:png_write_row
race:tzset_internal

# The residue that stays red, enumerated here so nobody re-derives it:
# QArrayData-region races between two of Qt 6.10.2's own 'Thread (pooled)'
# threads around image save/read, plus stripped libQt6Gui/libtbb offsets. They
# cannot be name-matched (stripped libraries) and must not be blanket-blinded
# (called_from_lib would hide every real app race through Qt). Reproduced
# without any qimgv code in ~/tsan-qthreadpool-check/qtimagepool.cpp — 30
# lines, QImage save + scaled read, same shape. Upstream's.
#
# Measured 2026-11-07, verified present at 0a9559ea as well (inherited, not
# introduced by the cancel / frame-name / shared-thumbnailer arcs): the same
# class reached through OUR WorkerPool threads — the memmove of a queued
# connection's arguments inside emit finished (LoaderRunnable::run) and
# taskStart delivery (Thumbnailer::onTaskStart), QArrayData::reallocateUnaligned,
# and cleanOrphanedConnectionsImpl during widget teardown. Qt's own container
# and connection internals race by TSan's lights; our frames are only the
# callers.
# Decided the same day, no longer deferred: the emit-path class reproduces
# with zero qimgv code in ~/tsan-qthreadpool-check/qsignals.cpp — 5/5 runs at
# libQt6Core+0x29c364, the exact offset the tree names. Upstream's, like the
# qtimagepool shape above. Deliberately unsuppressed: these names are the
# machinery every real race through Qt also travels, so matching them would
# blind the instrument exactly where it must stay sharp. The enumeration IS
# the record; any shape beyond it still fails the run.
